# LaTeX output: latexmk writes auxiliary files to build/ and each PDF next to its driver (main.tex, short.tex, brief.tex).
# The compiled versions (main.pdf, short.pdf, brief.pdf) are tracked so they can be read on GitHub; local copies such as
# preview_draft.pdf are not.
/build/
/*.pdf
!/main.pdf
!/short.pdf
!/brief.pdf
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.run.xml
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.xdv

# Generated assets (figures, tables, numbers) are tracked: the researcher approved publishing the report and
# everything it shows (2026-10-28), so a clone can rebuild the PDF without the participant data.
# The face-blurred spare photo is not used by the report.
/figures/photo/data_collection_blurred.jpg

# Python caches of scripts/
__pycache__/
